# Lattice ECP5 LFE5U-25F (CABGA256, speed grade 6) constraints for fpga_top.
#
# Target clock is 50 MHz (20 ns) -- the same CLOCK_PERIOD the SKY130
# OpenLane runs used (designs/accelerator_int*_parallel/config.json), so
# "does it meet the ASIC's clock target" is a like-for-like question.
# nextpnr still reports the achieved Fmax of the placed-and-routed design,
# which is the number results/metrics.csv records.
FREQUENCY PORT "clk" 50 MHZ;

# No LOCATE constraints on purpose: fpga_top exposes the accelerator's raw
# parallel host interface (~100 pins for INT8), which is not wired to any
# real board. nextpnr places the I/Os itself; the resulting bitstream is a
# fit/timing artifact, not a board-deployable image. A board build needs a
# serial (e.g. UART) front end that owns the host interface instead.
